 "findings": [
  "NDVI anomaly at county level is the strongest signal (oct1 corr +0.52 with log PPA ratio; TX +0.62), stronger than weather",
  "state-level fit on raw NDVI levels overfits (17 states x few years) and is worse than base",
  "March-intentions area adds ~6% mean TX error; June Acreage removes part of the handicap",
  "oct1 per-acre error 9.8% and abandonment years 2019/2020 captured (+3%/0%) where USDA Aug was +33%/+36%",
  "blend with USDA does not beat USDA (oct1 10.8 vs 11.0, noise); error corr 0.5-0.8",
  "revision signal weak: sep1 corr +0.28 with final/USDA_AUG, sign hit 0.57 (0.65 if gap>10%), 9 seasons -> not significant"
 ],
 "negative": "satellite+public weather does not beat USDA monthly forecasts in any cutoff on development years",
